== Usage ==
=== Minion Fuel ===
{{Affected Minions List|fuel|Inferno|table_header={{Item|Inferno Minion}}s only|table_list=n}} It lasts for 24 hours. 

The specialty and Rarity of an Inferno Minion Fuel is determined by the [[Distillates|Distillate]] and tier of [[Gabagool (disambiguation)|Gabagool]] used in its crafting recipe. The Distillate ({{Item|Magma Cream Distillate}}, {{Item|Blaze Rod Distillate}}, {{Item|Nether Wart Distillate}}, {{Item|Glowstone Distillate}}, or {{Item|Gabagool Distillate}}) used determines whether the Fuel has a specialty of {{Item|Magma Cream}}, {{Item|Blaze Rod}}, {{Item|Nether Wart}}, {{Item|Glowstone Dust}}, or {{Item|Crude Gabagool}}. The specialty item will be collected by the Minion 80% of time it makes a harvest. The tier of Gabagool ({{Item|Fuel Gabagool}}, {{Item|Heavy Gabagool}} or {{Item|Hypergolic Gabagool}}) used determines the speed boost of the fuel, with {{Rare}} giving {{Green|10x}}, {{Epic}} giving {{Green|15x}}, and {{Legendary}} giving {{Green|20x}} speed. 

=== {{Legendary}} Fuel drops ===
{{Legendary}} Fuel also gives the Minion a chance to produce {{Item|Chili Pepper}}s, {{Item|Inferno Vertex|text=Inferno Vertices}}, {{Item|Inferno Apex}}es, {{Item|Reaper Pepper}}s, and {{Item|Gabagool the Fish}}. For every harvesting action by the Minion, each rare drop is rolled, and can be generated by the minion.

; Drop Chances (per roll)
*Chili Pepper: {{Chance|0.7352941176%|1|136}}
*Inferno Vertex: {{Chance|0.0168067227%|1|5,950}}
*Inferno Apex: {{Chance|0.0000763889%|1|1,309,091}}
*Reaper Pepper: {{Chance|0.0002182539%|1|458,182}} 
*Gabagool the Fish: {{Chance|0.0000254629%|1|3,927,273}}

After expiring, {{Legendary}} fuel produces {{Item|Hypergolic Ionized Ceramics|amount=1}}.

== Bugs ==
* The speed multipliers are applied along with the other speed buffs to the base action time as follows:<math>\frac{\text{baseActionTime}}{(1 + \text{speedBuffs}) * (1 + \text{InfernoMinionFuelMultiplier})}</math>. This extra <math>1+</math> in front of the '''Inferno Minion Fuel''' multiplier causes the effective multipliers to be {{Green|11x}}, {{Green|16x}}, and {{Green|21x}}.

